insert into public.evidence (id, response_id, kind, strength, title, source, note) values
('5ae9ca3c-c96e-5142-b684-5db5e0542daf'::uuid, 'c17b15c8-b808-595b-a5e3-b86125a7db6f'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'EO covers both the CDRRMO and BDRRMOs and follows minimum requirements; amended, but no ordinance on BDRRMOs.'),
('2b7458fd-1a5a-5eb3-a04f-08a5b2664b18'::uuid, 'c17b15c8-b808-595b-a5e3-b86125a7db6f'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan lists hiring of 4+4+2 CDRRMO plantilla positions, so the office is not yet staffed as a full department.'),
('1aeedb80-354e-5afd-bbcf-debd52206ab3'::uuid, 'c17b15c8-b808-595b-a5e3-b86125a7db6f'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) none of the 23 City issuances creates the CDRRMO as a regular department. CDP 2024-2030 Vol. 2 Table 17 PPAs 1.1.1-1.1.2 commit to creating regular positions for the CDRRMO complement, an Admin Officer and a Property Custodian; SP Res. 2023-347 records the CDRRMO''s "lack of manpower for emergency and disaster response".'),
('2bf94a94-a0d8-502c-b977-23820765dc90'::uuid, '012a93b7-515f-579e-b82d-b686e69e176d'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'CDRRMC EO needs updating to cover the mandated representations; minimum of 4 CSO seats not yet met.'),
('cc4713da-a123-555f-a3a0-737069c07a41'::uuid, '012a93b7-515f-579e-b82d-b686e69e176d'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) EO No. 2024-032A (July 2024, reviewed by City Legal 1 Jul 2024) reorganises the CDRRMC and supersedes EO 2023-0041 (16 May 2023). It lists the Mayor (chair), Vice Mayor, SP committee chairs on CCA-DRRM and public safety, Liga president, City Administrator, CDRRMO, CPDO, Budget, Accountant, CHO, CSWD, Agriculture, Engineering, Waterworks, Veterinary, CGSO, ENRO, IPGDO (GAD), DOH-CHD HEMS, DILG, DepEd SDO, DPWH, PA 802nd Bde, 8RCDG ARESCOM, PNP, BFP, PCG, PN reserve, PPA, PRC, 5 CSOs and 2 private-sector seats (EDC Leyte Geothermal, LEYECO V; a 3rd seat is blank). Proof of use: 2024-2025 CDRRMC resolutions are moved and seconded by member offices (DepEd, PNP, PCG, CSWD, Waterworks, CGSO, Engineering, CHO, a CSO). [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('d89b4319-d30b-5f43-a21c-69000f843226'::uuid, '283b7870-a4bb-57b5-b913-ba65abab616f'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 4 (quarterly meetings, minutes and resolutions on file).'),
('d6f0b534-ae35-5745-8a97-8a0664b5bbfe'::uuid, '283b7870-a4bb-57b5-b913-ba65abab616f'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'CDRRMC Res. No. 1 s.2023 approved the 10-Yr Plan. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('45c2d4b4-b334-5f54-88b0-5f7367a6978b'::uuid, '283b7870-a4bb-57b5-b913-ba65abab616f'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) resolutions sighted from the 4th Quarter meeting of 29 Nov 2024 (Res. 09, 10 s.2024), the 2nd Quarter meeting of 26 Jun 2025 (Res. 01-03 s.2025), a 3rd Quarter special meeting of 30 Sep 2025 (Res. 05), a special meeting of 8 Nov 2025 for Typhoon Tino (Res. 06) and a meeting of 20 Nov 2025 (Res. 07, 08). Res. 04 s.2025 is undated ("this __ day of November 2025") and repeats control no. 2025-07-180. EO 2024-032A Sec. 2(d) sets the quarterly schedule. No minutes or attendance sheets, and no 1st Quarter 2025 record, were in the set. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('08ca6026-057e-5c2c-b779-2d8c06d7b300'::uuid, '33dca86b-ac84-535f-a6f3-585766be3912'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 4; CDRRMO serves as secretariat.'),
('4893fb60-fd81-57e1-bade-4c1150678d02'::uuid, '33dca86b-ac84-535f-a6f3-585766be3912'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) the CDRRMO Head certifies CDRRMC Res. 01-06 s.2025 as Secretariat; the resolutions follow one excerpt-of-minutes format with CDRRMO control numbers (e.g., CDRRMO-2025-07-178) and transmittal lists to the SP, Budget, Accounting, CPDO, DILG and OCD VIII. Lapses: Res. 04 s.2025 undated and with a reused control number; Res. 07 and 08 s.2025 carry no Secretariat certification; Res. 05 has no series year in its number. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('a12d004d-9663-5ca5-b63b-7d8ea695f8d0'::uuid, 'b9af8f93-7828-5b7d-bf4d-9e3d2760f414'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'pre-emptive/forced evacuation ordinance in force but needs amendment; granular class suspension needed.'),
('abb64876-77cd-560a-b38c-338538b4da29'::uuid, 'b9af8f93-7828-5b7d-bf4d-9e3d2760f414'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'CLUP/ZO 2017-2027 in force with Water Code river easements, a 5-m easement on the Marina Fault trace and no-build zones, but no flood, landslide or storm-surge overlay zone (its overlays are heritage, critical habitat, eco-tourism, KBA, TOD and urban corridor). 10-Yr Plan cites an approved Shelter Plan. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('0adac076-d9a0-5f48-8647-80c09be3e08c'::uuid, 'b9af8f93-7828-5b7d-bf4d-9e3d2760f414'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(issuances 2021-2024, read 6 Nov 2026) CDRRMC Res. 09 s.2021 (15 Dec 2021, Odette) directed all barangays to start pre-emptive evacuation of high-risk residents; Res. 08 s.2021 (Odette) and Res. 06 s.2022 (TD Agaton, 13 Apr 2022, citing DepEd Order 66 s.2012) suspended work and classes. These show the council uses the evacuation and suspension rules, event by event. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('1b6fc579-efcb-5e65-8a69-08ac20fcf29a'::uuid, '5b1a42b2-d11d-535f-a8e9-c0aa9e59b0c0'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 4, ''innate in the policy''; confusion noted on national declarations (e.g., San Juanico Bridge closure).'),
('e01c4368-990a-5535-9728-e1050a9b02c0'::uuid, '5b1a42b2-d11d-535f-a8e9-c0aa9e59b0c0'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan records a State of Calamity declaration (Res. No. 354) for TS Urduja 2017. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('a491a0bf-02c0-5ceb-bb97-fcdfe39feb94'::uuid, '5b1a42b2-d11d-535f-a8e9-c0aa9e59b0c0'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) CDRRMC Res. 03 s.2025 (26 Jun 2025) adopts Presidential Proclamation No. 920 (State of Calamity, Region VIII, San Juanico Bridge) and cites the LDRRMF; Res. 01 s.2025 cites the same regional declaration. Res. 06 s.2025 (8 Nov 2025) approves PHP 2.0 M from the 30% QRF for Typhoon Tino (Kalmaegi) relief but does not cite the declaration it relies on, although Res. 05 s.2025 states the QRF is "only utilized upon declaration of a state of calamity". CDP 2024-2030 PPA 3.1.1 lists "Declaration of State of Calamity" under the QRF programme. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('d486f0ea-736f-50eb-8098-991527e461fa'::uuid, '5b1a42b2-d11d-535f-a8e9-c0aa9e59b0c0'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(issuances 2021-2024, read 6 Nov 2026) SP Res. 2021-366 adopted the State of Calamity for Typhoon Odette (16 Dec 2021); CDRRMC Res. 06 s.2024 recommended a State of Calamity for the dengue outbreak, capped at one year and liftable on the council''s recommendation, with CHD tasks. Two more cases of the protocol in use; still no written stand-alone protocol. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('1bd26372-9d0e-56d0-ab1b-67be6b2c6e31'::uuid, '1d9cddd8-8636-5604-afde-e262e4c2b76d'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 4; DRRM represented in CDC and LFC.'),
('0ae853cb-6cdc-58b7-af14-b8ada737eb2c'::uuid, '1d9cddd8-8636-5604-afde-e262e4c2b76d'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) SP Res. 2024-088 (19 Mar 2024) records that the Trust Fund-LDRRMF 2024 Budget Program and Investment Plan went through a budget plan review by CPDO, the City Budget Office and the City Accountant (LFC member offices) before SP adoption; CDP 2024-2030 Vol. 2 Sec. C.1 carries a full CCA-DRRM sub-sector with 5 programmes, showing DRRM input into the CDC plan. EO 2024-032A Sec. 2(b) tasks the CDRRMC to integrate DRR-CCA into development plans and budgets. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('b2f65428-ef0b-5210-81c6-9f2399cece53'::uuid, '6e0cc231-acc4-5131-b65b-41df583596eb'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'RA 12287 IRR signed 14 Sep 2026;'),
('b69c745f-8837-5a74-a198-450b0e71b9f0'::uuid, '6e0cc231-acc4-5131-b65b-41df583596eb'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', '(A4.6) AA arrangements ''not in place yet at local level, IRR for cascading''. No local SID SOP, EO template or RDRRMC request template found.'),
('895b3202-ed6a-56fd-bc8b-82bee582ea3a'::uuid, '2156dae5-216b-53a3-9128-b76554891d9b'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 2.'),
('e596267c-d6fc-5283-ba8a-e77267f53b8e'::uuid, '2156dae5-216b-53a3-9128-b76554891d9b'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan SWOC says required CDRRMO positions exist but are not filled; FGDs show Planning, Operations and Admin sections exist.'),
('bcc54e4f-4a13-5f9e-a90e-dcaa9bf71eef'::uuid, '7981b083-b30f-519a-9a28-04f3cbab2ee4'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 4; permanent Head appointed.'),
('a6e7a599-b1f7-5943-b4be-14972e947d6b'::uuid, '7981b083-b30f-519a-9a28-04f3cbab2ee4'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan names the CDRRMO Head. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('b61e93fe-d927-5640-b86e-d8932b8579e0'::uuid, '4614955e-cace-5e8f-9e3c-dcb79cb1e1f9'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 4.'),
('eae8ce50-5f54-5c14-87eb-ee78f795e608'::uuid, '4614955e-cace-5e8f-9e3c-dcb79cb1e1f9'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan SWOC says required positions are not filled and its PPAs include hiring 4+4+2 plantilla items plus a maintenance engineer and property custodian.'),
('18f3b950-cc19-5877-aaa9-8f0cf309be2f'::uuid, '4614955e-cace-5e8f-9e3c-dcb79cb1e1f9'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) CDP 2024-2030 PPAs 1.1.1-1.1.2 (create regular positions for the CDRRMO complement; fill Admin Officer and Property Custodian), 1.2.4, 1.6.2 and 1.15.4 (regular positions for EWS, structural assessment and CDRA database) and 2.1.3 (risk communications) confirm that the posts are still to be created. SP Res. 2023-347 records the CDRRMO''s lack of response manpower.'),
('adb696c1-98e6-5213-9176-66ab747a796d'::uuid, '732a471b-7b05-5894-ae14-1cc993d8713f'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 2. Admin FGD: ''clearer job description per staff''; no monitoring tool for individual performance.'),
('b0a05605-0b72-5ad8-9be3-6e29e6eec47b'::uuid, 'ab53dfc9-1973-50e5-87dc-c8d208d32bb6'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'attached SOP covers EOC activation only, not an SP-approved OpCen SOP for normal operations.'),
('125eee80-0a62-5578-b90e-24b51432bf99'::uuid, 'ab53dfc9-1973-50e5-87dc-c8d208d32bb6'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan says the Operations Center runs 24/7 with trained personnel, but operations need a manual/SOP; ''Operations Center SOP/Manual'' is a 2023-24 PPA.'),
('a3d4cc2a-2d29-552b-a3d2-9f4f9f1a6771'::uuid, 'ab53dfc9-1973-50e5-87dc-c8d208d32bb6'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) CDP 2024-2030 PPA 2.10.3 "Formulation of Operations Center SOP/Manual" (programme 2.10 Ormoc City DRRM Operations Center) confirms the SOP is still to be written; strategy 2 plans an Ormoc City Integrated Operation Center and Emergency Hotline.'),
('75235cc3-a53e-5fc9-8ff3-c10e93f3cb5b'::uuid, 'ab53dfc9-1973-50e5-87dc-c8d208d32bb6'::uuid, 'observation', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Site observation, October 2026', 'Assessment team site visit', '(Oct 2026 site visit) 24-hour duty is in operation at the CDRRM Office for the City''s three priority areas: City Traffic Monitoring, Public Safety and Emergency Monitoring. Score 1 -> 2: the practice is observed, but there is no approved normal-operations SOP or signed roster (a 3 needs both).'),
('bfc42752-3e55-503d-a0bb-f78fd1b9b41f'::uuid, '9bf9db95-0edb-5da0-8eef-d3e3d892003b'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 1. Planning FGD: no training needs assessment plan; Admin FGD: TNA proposals not routed to Planning.'),
('a46de630-0558-5473-bd0b-8921de3ecc88'::uuid, '9bf9db95-0edb-5da0-8eef-d3e3d892003b'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan lists ICS all levels, EOC Management, MDM, CCCM, RDANA and PDNA training.'),
('773f6087-e5ed-5323-aa22-2be7cc4db456'::uuid, '9bf9db95-0edb-5da0-8eef-d3e3d892003b'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) CDRRMC Res. 09 s.2024 directs the CDRRMO to train city and barangay officials and responders on ICS; CDP 2024-2030 PPAs 1.1.6 (standard training modules) and 2.6.1-2.6.3 (capacity building for CDRRMC agencies and BDRRMCs, local pool of trainers, simulation exercises). Still no TNA.'),
('78605d31-d9bd-5dc1-9214-21d52c845bcc'::uuid, '694e80ca-fd79-5b7a-8168-b48c0fc42f56'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 1.'),
('feb28d00-bfe4-5774-82d8-f4b32d2747f3'::uuid, '694e80ca-fd79-5b7a-8168-b48c0fc42f56'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan lists responder care and insurance for ACDVs as planned PPAs.'),
('4b5b6dc7-f8d2-5eb3-8ecd-dcbecbacb679'::uuid, '694e80ca-fd79-5b7a-8168-b48c0fc42f56'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(issuances 2021-2024, read 6 Nov 2026) CDRRMC Res. 03 and 04 s.2022 (31 Mar 2022) adopt NDRRMC MC 64 s.2021 on accreditation, mobilisation and protection of community disaster volunteers, and approve a risk categorisation as the basis for buying insurance for accredited volunteers. Score 1 -> 2: an approved basis exists for volunteer insurance; no policy, staff insurance, hazard pay, PPE issue list or MHPSS arrangement was sighted.'),
('c3e83204-4e9e-50c9-828a-054cc9715d83'::uuid, '4ea14592-7a60-5788-adad-55ccc1d630c5'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 3.'),
('978c8049-4207-5f66-aeb7-97331d774fef'::uuid, '4ea14592-7a60-5788-adad-55ccc1d630c5'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan SWOC says the volunteer roster is not institutionalised; ACDV roster/accreditation is a planned PPA. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('ebf471bf-f5fe-5918-81b3-5c02bdf28d18'::uuid, '4ea14592-7a60-5788-adad-55ccc1d630c5'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) SP Res. 2023-347 (29 Dec 2023) authorises the MOA with CPR-RIMT Rapid Rescue Rider Ormoc Chapter, a City-accredited CSO whose members are "CDRRMO accredited community disaster volunteers"; under the MOA the CSO augments HEMS and the CDRRMO (incl. mass casualty) and post-disaster operations, the CDRRMO trains and supplies them, HEMS supervises them in operations and the City is accountable for volunteer injury or loss. The CSO sits on the CDRRMC (EO 2024-032A) and the El Nino Task Force (EO 2023-0042). The MOA copy in the set is unsigned and not notarised. CDP PPAs 2.7.1-2.7.3 plan the ACDV roster, insurance premiums and training. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('9b40afef-cf07-59e8-b5b1-4d25810d8392'::uuid, '4ea14592-7a60-5788-adad-55ccc1d630c5'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(issuances 2021-2024, read 6 Nov 2026) CDRRMC Res. 03/04 s.2022 adopt NDRRMC MC 64 s.2021 (ACDV accreditation, mobilisation, protection) and an insurance risk categorisation. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('b4322a40-8cf7-55ce-bcc2-4b6578673bd1'::uuid, '2a1edad2-9fd7-57eb-a34e-0df53d86c11b'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'no AA focal-person designation found in the documents reviewed;'),
('94641488-0b60-5315-b446-c5c39924165f'::uuid, '2a1edad2-9fd7-57eb-a34e-0df53d86c11b'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', '(A4.6) AA not yet in place locally.'),
('f6bea802-3953-5b51-8827-94b406e00d43'::uuid, 'd198a40b-8c44-51e5-83ea-50becadd0f7a'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', '(Admin FGD, formerly under A1.3) lack of a database on personnel.'),
('0cae2b1a-c423-52a8-abaf-2e76e79ba2a7'::uuid, 'd198a40b-8c44-51e5-83ea-50becadd0f7a'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan volunteer roster not institutionalised.'),
('d57c0bcc-98a4-5ee1-9822-3faa54d1326c'::uuid, 'a3561a08-069e-5542-9ffd-0d7ca99b62e6'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 4.'),
('5884421c-da95-5811-add4-05caa6ea5b67'::uuid, 'a3561a08-069e-5542-9ffd-0d7ca99b62e6'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan adopted by SP Res. 2023-112, prepared with the NDRRMC 2022 LDRRMP guidebook. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('411860f2-3848-5e2f-816d-14365f391a3d'::uuid, 'a3561a08-069e-5542-9ffd-0d7ca99b62e6'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) SP Res. 2023-112 (adopted 24 Apr 2023) sighted: the SP adopts the Ormoc City DRRM Ten-Year Plan 2023-2032 on the Mayor''s endorsement of 20 Feb 2023, after CDRRMC Res. No. 01 s.2023 (17 Feb 2023). EO 2024-032A Sec. 2(a) tasks the CDRRMC to approve, monitor, evaluate and regularly review and test the LDRRMP. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('f6306893-403b-5aa2-940f-b0f72e678915'::uuid, '4802802d-6669-51ed-a1ae-51b54830b004'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'plans mainstreaming and provisions need review.'),
('8d7a33a5-feab-544c-a4e8-be805fc4ba20'::uuid, '4802802d-6669-51ed-a1ae-51b54830b004'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'CLUP 2017-2027 has a DRRM-CCA sectoral chapter and fault/river easements, but no hazard overlay zones; it still uses 110 barangays and predates the CDRA. CDRA Final Report (TWG under EO 2023-0025) Ch.6 sets 8 Major Decision Areas to feed the CLUP, ZO, CDP, LCCAP, LDRRMP and LDRRMFIP.'),
('58f4adfe-6e61-5968-8d0e-373b6c0ab2bb'::uuid, '4802802d-6669-51ed-a1ae-51b54830b004'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) CDP 2024-2030 Vol. 2 Sec. C.1 (CCA-DRRM sub-sector, pp.197-213) sets goals, objectives and 5 programmes and names the CDRA database as "basis for all development planning"; LCCAP 2019-2030 is built on a CDRA (HLURB method) with RCP 8.5 projections, a GHG inventory and decision areas, and lists the LCCAP as CDP project no. 22. Weaknesses: the CDP still targets "110 barangays", the LCCAP predates the 2023 CDRA and the 10-Year Plan, and no LCCAP-LDRRMP crosswalk exists.'),
('258064ed-a98b-5435-859f-9ac9d381b815'::uuid, '4802802d-6669-51ed-a1ae-51b54830b004'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(issuances 2021-2024, read 6 Nov 2026) The Flood Control and Drainage Improvement Master Plan and Feasibility Study was funded by CDRRMC Res. 03 s.2023 (18 May 2023, PHP 3.60 M from the CCTV line of the 5% LDRRMF 2023), Res. 04 s.2023 (May 2023, PHP 3.11 M reverted continuing capital outlay 2017-2022) and Res. 07 s.2023 (12 Dec 2023, a further PHP 4.31 M of unobligated 2023 balances). No contract, inception report or finished study was sighted, and the CDP still lists the drainage master plan as planned (PPA 2.12).'),
('617d5e9b-0076-5f18-be8a-841db2f77cf6'::uuid, '4e61821a-2091-527b-9fc9-a1999f4a6b6d'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'CPs updated but tested only for earthquake and flooding.'),
('33fa3a36-125b-5328-a923-4f6983994c3f'::uuid, '4e61821a-2091-527b-9fc9-a1999f4a6b6d'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan says CPs exist but need updating; new CPs are planned. CDRA MDA 7 calls for hazard-specific CPs for flood, landslide, storm surge, earthquake and tsunami. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('bf3d13c1-f440-5504-99bf-6d088cb33953'::uuid, '4e61821a-2091-527b-9fc9-a1999f4a6b6d'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) CDP 2024-2030 PPA 2.4 (city and barangay contingency plans) and 2.21 (El Nino programme); EO 2023-0042 (19 May 2023) creates the El Nino Task Force and tasks it to formulate a preparedness and rehabilitation plan, which was not in the set. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('6df268ff-27d0-5948-b254-f6bab8a90102'::uuid, '4e61821a-2091-527b-9fc9-a1999f4a6b6d'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(issuances 2021-2024, read 6 Nov 2026) CDRRMC Res. 2-A s.2021 adopted the Enhanced Contingency Plan for flood-affected barangays ("Oplan Lunop") and Res. 2-B s.2021 the Enhanced CP for Earthquake 2020-2025, both with COVID-19 protocols (3 May 2021), and sent them to the SP for approval. SP approval not sighted. The earthquake CP''s period ended in 2025, so it is due for update. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('fa7c2bd0-e5c5-5dbe-a52b-8b663a6c5d5a'::uuid, '80aca07c-2c0a-5c9b-8852-391f75e17315'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 2.'),
('f6556a2f-6592-5905-b01f-19e9ca6a33a5'::uuid, '80aca07c-2c0a-5c9b-8852-391f75e17315'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'PSCP formulation is a 2023 PPA in 10-Yr Plan; NDRRMC/OCD PSCP Guidebook available.'),
('397b6442-f182-56fe-a6a4-a8cb1e72158c'::uuid, '80aca07c-2c0a-5c9b-8852-391f75e17315'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) CDP 2024-2030 PPA 2.5 plans PSCP formulation and institutionalisation; no PSCP in the set.'),
('c5c0f865-3a58-5cba-be74-03d4b9a46bd7'::uuid, '62050213-3f6c-5c1b-ad96-ffc96cb10a76'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 4; LDRRMFIP prepared and approved.'),
('1421cb19-b6a0-53bc-a9cb-65bba6f5bce5'::uuid, '62050213-3f6c-5c1b-ad96-ffc96cb10a76'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan includes a 10-year LDRRMFIP of PHP 14.63 B (80% construction; 52% digital governance) with no anticipatory action line. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('b6214a65-aa90-5422-a0fa-29861075a3a8'::uuid, '62050213-3f6c-5c1b-ad96-ffc96cb10a76'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) annual cycle shown: SP Res. 2024-088 (19 Mar 2024) adopts CDRRMC Res. 3 s.2024 approving the Trust Fund-LDRRMF 2024 Budget Program and Investment Plan (PHP 79,512,680.20) after CPDO/Budget/Accountant review; CDRRMC Res. 01 s.2025 approves the LDRRMIP Trust Fund CY2025 (PHP 52,713,712.18); Res. 05 s.2025 (30 Sep 2025) approves the 5% LDRRMF CY2026 Budget Program and Investment Plan (PHP 139,955,741.40); Res. 07 s.2025 endorses a supplemental PHP 493,550.11 and Res. 08 s.2025 reallocates PHP 2.0 M of the 2025 Trust Fund to drainage in Brgy South. SP approval of the CY2026 plan was not in the set. Res. 05 calls the plan CY2026 but its body cites the 2025 NTA and "LDRRMF CY 2025". No AA line. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('5b79647f-d6d1-59d5-8878-c9f472f72bd6'::uuid, '32ad7cea-17c7-50c7-b639-631673e3aba0'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'incomplete.'),
('04bc873d-f172-5a7b-881b-45b10d8a391b'::uuid, '32ad7cea-17c7-50c7-b639-631673e3aba0'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan lists EC database/geotagging and Operation L!sto manual as PPAs; 46 barangays are critical flood barangays.'),
('7b385c59-3f76-56fb-8037-7f5ced2bf45a'::uuid, '32ad7cea-17c7-50c7-b639-631673e3aba0'::uuid, 'observation', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Site observation, October 2026', 'Assessment team site visit', '(Oct 2026 site visit) one flood-prone barangay visited has an established evacuation site and an evacuation protocol. One barangay does not yet show city-wide coverage (46 critical flood barangays), so the score stays 2.'),
('9a7e3b16-ab28-53c5-8265-1c3c7535fbc0'::uuid, 'e327b421-ea9c-5038-9f7f-9357f6b96c0f'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'SGLG-type compliance with good practice.'),
('e4885a91-5ee1-559b-9273-271b3207bfb6'::uuid, 'e327b421-ea9c-5038-9f7f-9357f6b96c0f'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) EO 2023-0085 (29 Dec 2023) creates the Barangay DRRM Plan Review Team (CDRRMO Head as team leader, CPDO assistant team leader; CSWD, CHD-HEMS, IPGDO, ENRO, Liga, two CSOs; DILG CLGOO oversight). It adopts the Enhanced QAS for BDRRMP/C (NDRRMC MC 03 s.2022), checks barangay PAPs against hazards and the barangay AIP, issues a Certificate of Review and copies DILG within 3 days. No Certificates of Review or status matrix were in the set. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('d6c80f86-c1e3-5d7d-965d-ac78f0f63ce4'::uuid, 'e1800441-4564-5a86-9813-92c3d72de086'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 4.'),
('c4527e6c-ae03-5480-bc89-e6fa7854c187'::uuid, 'e1800441-4564-5a86-9813-92c3d72de086'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) CDRRMC Res. 05 s.2025 sets the CY2026 LDRRMF at PHP 139,955,741.40, stated as 5% "based on the total National Tax Allotment of the City"; Res. 03 s.2025 and SP Res. 2024-088 cite RA 10121 Sec. 21 / IRR Rule 18. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('063cc23e-02b5-5f62-9ecc-076359fe2888'::uuid, '51b90def-3147-54ab-a71a-97b0e033d117'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 4.'),
('025c5669-1c34-5c40-8bb5-8dede3f32024'::uuid, '51b90def-3147-54ab-a71a-97b0e033d117'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) CDRRMC Res. 05 s.2025 allocates PHP 97,969,018.98 (70%) to prevention-mitigation, preparedness, response and recovery and PHP 41,986,722.42 (30%) to the QRF; Res. 07 s.2025 splits a supplemental share 30/70 (QRF PHP 148,065.03; mitigation and preparedness PHP 345,485.08). [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
