('ea600d54-825d-54eb-ab17-fd128f80a741'::uuid, 'cbee3855-118c-52f2-8301-83cd669c6703'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) SP Res. 2024-088 adopts the Trust Fund-LDRRMF 2024 plan (PHP 79,512,680.20) and cites RA 10121 Sec. 21 (5-year use) and COA Circular 2012-002 Sec. 4.4; CDRRMC Res. 01 s.2025 approves the CY2025 Trust Fund plan (PHP 52,713,712.18); Res. 08 s.2025 reallocates PHP 2.0 M of it to a drainage project after City Accountant advice that CDRRMC approval and SP concurrence are needed. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('e18c0505-595a-5213-9c77-dc5b35d8b564'::uuid, '2e056aca-2637-522c-91b6-069aa6e1a801'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', '80% utilisation not yet met; monitoring needed.'),
('1d140d3f-c6fa-52c2-99b5-c39dec7177c5'::uuid, '2e056aca-2637-522c-91b6-069aa6e1a801'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan SWOC notes QRF utilisation/accessibility is a challenge.'),
('1eed3923-3af6-51ed-bf5f-f9750555dfe3'::uuid, '2e056aca-2637-522c-91b6-069aa6e1a801'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) Trust Fund balances of PHP 79.5 M (2024 plan) and PHP 52.7 M (CY2025 plan) show sizeable unexpended LDRRMF carried forward; Res. 06 s.2025 draws PHP 2.0 M from the QRF for Typhoon Tino. No utilisation report was in the set.'),
('6d6b476c-0f0f-5f59-8905-49ba18bccad1'::uuid, '97831d29-05c4-5bf1-b4d4-23c058cc124c'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'local suppliers'' capability needs regular updating.'),
('6f25f896-6537-502b-ba09-a8d1eb7f2703'::uuid, '88c9dbde-603a-5b23-a4cd-4882ef0fb4e6'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'not in place locally; awaiting IRR cascading.'),
('0967c5c5-4bcf-554f-b55c-3d7fe52047a6'::uuid, '88c9dbde-603a-5b23-a4cd-4882ef0fb4e6'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'IRR Rule V allows up to 10% of the 70% LDRRMF for AA; <=30% more than 3 days before impact, up to 70% within 3 days. DBM-COA guidelines pending.'),
('759d40c9-b6f3-5fe1-8630-97d1f37f9179'::uuid, '88c9dbde-603a-5b23-a4cd-4882ef0fb4e6'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) the CY2026 LDRRMF plan (Res. 05 s.2025, 30 Sep 2025) predates the IRR and has no AA line. CDP 2024-2030 PPA 3.15 "Risk and forecast-based Financing Support Program" and PPA 1.1.7 (FNFI prepositioning for imminent threat) give a programme hook for the AA line.'),
('50858a27-97eb-58f5-ae71-4f5c58d0f5b2'::uuid, '7114b994-82b1-5ed5-9135-499924a1cbc2'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 3.'),
('34bb164f-ecf5-5213-b95c-6e5f3f284579'::uuid, '7114b994-82b1-5ed5-9135-499924a1cbc2'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'CDRA reports that only 15% of critical-point facilities are insured and that no lifeline utility is insured. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('5100a1bc-c2ef-5888-b798-5d8fc9cf617e'::uuid, '7114b994-82b1-5ed5-9135-499924a1cbc2'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) CDP 2024-2030 PPAs 1.3 (Disaster Risk Financing Program, incl. insurance of equipment, buildings and vital assets) and 1.2.3 (insure EWS devices); LCCAP 2019-2030 activity 3 enlists all 4,540 registered farmers in crop insurance (10% then unregistered). [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('064ebe35-a2ac-50b1-a9ba-c9d5f7e55d40'::uuid, '48303372-fc90-5312-bfc4-00985b4b0432'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'internal audit to be ensured.'),
('d8d49077-d463-5e41-b7b4-f8cbc230a6d3'::uuid, 'bb946818-cda4-5a4a-9f8e-71e90ad31286'::uuid, 'document', 'partial'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '10-Yr Plan (GeoRiskPH) gives potential asset damage by hazard (flood PHP 222.4 B; rain-induced landslide PHP 205.5 B; liquefaction PHP 189.3 B; tsunami PHP 59.0 B). CLUP set the QRF at PHP 13.99 M (2017 figure). No costed response scenario compared with QRF/STF found; 10-Yr Plan SWOC notes QRF access is a challenge.'),
('fdd35cc1-4042-5c21-bd31-6c6fde0f3082'::uuid, 'cc6fb7f3-7e53-51af-9daa-122c2e3b7c51'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'scored 3.'),
('a7ba4ece-463c-57f7-9ab5-387e359ae186'::uuid, 'cc6fb7f3-7e53-51af-9daa-122c2e3b7c51'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'GeoRiskPH MOA with PHIVOLCS covers 6 hazards (10-Yr Plan). [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('a353c63c-5afd-5c1f-8202-e10696d250f3'::uuid, 'cc6fb7f3-7e53-51af-9daa-122c2e3b7c51'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) LCCAP 2019-2030 includes risk and susceptibility maps for flood, landslide, storm surge, earthquake, liquefaction and tsunami; the 2022 Ecological Profile (CDP Vol. 1) maps flood, landslide, ground shaking, liquefaction, rain-induced landslide and storm surge (SSA 1-4). Both predate the 85-barangay boundaries or use the old barangay base. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('91d46b46-7377-51b7-97e1-97f6ffc7d5bc'::uuid, '3c7cd8e5-365c-5250-9266-88d8a9d27ab6'::uuid, 'fgd', 'verbal'::public.evidence_strength, 'CDRRMO field self-assessment (FGD), October 2026', 'CDRRMO section FGDs', 'CDRA for updating.'),
('3382d7e6-7118-50d3-9bb2-2fa395b5e586'::uuid, '3c7cd8e5-365c-5250-9266-88d8a9d27ab6'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', 'CDRA Final Report (TWG under EO 2023-0025) reviewed: exposure, vulnerability and risk for flood, rain-induced landslide and storm surge across population, urban use areas, production areas, critical-point facilities and lifelines in 85 barangays, plus climate impact chains and Ch.6 policy interventions. Earthquake, liquefaction and tsunami are cited from GeoRiskPH figures, not assessed. [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
('cb6fce2d-13de-5941-b3f7-4780b28f7e1f'::uuid, '3c7cd8e5-365c-5250-9266-88d8a9d27ab6'::uuid, 'document', 'approved_in_use'::public.evidence_strength, 'Desk review, October-November 2026', 'Consultant desk review', '(doc review 6 Nov 2026) EO 2023-0025 (8 Mar 2023) creates the CDRA Technical Working Group (CPDO, CDRRMO, CSWD, Agriculture, ENRO, Engineering, CGSO, HEMS, Waterworks and 7 other offices, with DILG, DPWH, LEYECO V, NGCP, EDC, VSU and NRC as partners) to produce an updated CDRA and database, hazard and risk maps and to update them every 3-5 years. An earlier CDRA underpins the LCCAP 2019-2030 (TWG under EO No. 50 s.2017). [Imported at "approved and in use" from the assessor''s score. Attach the document and proof of use, or lower the strength, at validation.]'),
